    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5194/egusphere-2026-517",
    "abstract": "Abstract. Hawkins and Sutton (2009) developed a framework to partition total uncertainty in future climate projections into three components: internal variability, model uncertainty and scenario uncertainty. Here, we propose an extension of this framework that separates the contributions of global and regional processes. This enables a more physically based interpretation and improved understanding of the origins of projection uncertainty.",
    "field": "Climate projection uncertainty",
    "problem": "The established Hawkins and Sutton (2009) framework for partitioning climate projection uncertainty does not distinguish between contributions from global and regional processes, which hinders a more physically-based interpretation and understanding of the origins of regional climate uncertainty.",
    "method": "The proposed method extends the Hawkins and Sutton (2009) framework by using a Matched Global Warming technique to align model projections, thereby separating total climate projection uncertainty into distinct contributions from global and regional processes.",
    "task": "The task is to propose an extension to an existing framework to separate and quantify the contributions of global and regional processes to the total uncertainty in future climate change projections.",
    "model": [
        "CMIP6",
        "CMIP5"
    ],
